In view of the aforesaid discussion and being conscious of the settled position of law, the Court is of the considered view that the principle of double jeopardy does not apply to the present case and therefore, the learned court below did not commit any wrong or legal error in taking cognizance of the offences punishable under Sections 323 and 342 read with 34 IPC.
